  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday night through next Friday)\nIssued at 109 PM CDT Fri May 29 2026\n\nMainly a dry forecast this weekend, as short wave ridging aloft\nprevails across the Southern Plains. However, cannot rule out an \nisolated thunderstorm across the northern Edwards Plateau \n(Crockett County) early Sunday evening, as models show a weak \ndisturbance over the area. Otherwise, Sunday into Monday looks \ndry and hot, with afternoon highs ranging from the upper 90s to \nnear 100 degrees across the Big Country, to the lower and middle \n90s elsewhere. \n\nRain chances will increase across the area beginning Tuesday and \npersisting through much of the week, as southwest flow aloft \ndevelops across West Texas. Periodic disturbances moving through\nthe flow aloft will allow for low to medium rain chances\n(30%-50%) Tuesday through the rest of the work week. Temperatures \nwill also be cooler, with highs back in the 80s by mid to late \nweek.",
